# netlat's benchmark (devplan/bench.md §12), installed in share/bench by dist/netlat. It needs a
# wired host running tools/netlat-reflector; tools/bmds-bench starts one and gives peer= itself.

[Bench net.latency]
Exec=netlat --bench
Tags=peer
Help=Real-time UDP to a reflector and back, stamped in hardware: each stage's percentiles
Param.peer=;The reflector's IPv4 address (none: skipped)
Param.seconds=5;How long a run sends
Param.interval=1000;Microseconds between datagrams
Param.size=300;A datagram's payload, bytes
Param.fast=1;1: the real-time fast path; 0: through lwIP
Param.load=0;1: TCP both ways through the reflector meanwhile
Param.rt=0;The sender and receiver SCHED_FIFO at this priority (0: not real-time)
Param.runs=1;Runs (each one thousands of datagrams)
Param.warmup=0;Runs first, not kept
